1. Introduction

Wireshark is a network analysis tool used to capture and study data packets travelling through a network. It helps us understand how computers communicate with each other over the internet.

Wireshark displays information about network packets, such as source IP address, destination IP address, protocol, packet length and time.

It supports different protocols like TCP, UDP, DNS, HTTP and HTTPS. These protocols are used for different types of network communication.

Wireshark provides filters that help users find specific packets without checking all the captured data. By applying filters, we can easily identify the type of communication happening in a network.

In this experiment, different Wireshark filters are applied to analyze network traffic. The filters used are IP Address Filter, DNS Port Filter, HTTPS Port Filter and HTTP Port Filter.

These filters help us understand how devices communicate, how domain names are converted into IP addresses and how websites exchange data with users.

